{"kind":"request","text":"Review the observability design, Draft 2, at 4f0057ac (branch planner/observability-design, on origin/main 013fac7a): notes/2026-10-12-observability-design.md. Section 9 maps the five corrections of 12fc5d1a: (1) section 4.6 health reads the register by the deployment's configured registerScope through an internal readiness probe that is not a read and carries no data, validates sessions with sessionsOf (32-byte secret, deployment name), 2 s timeout, 5 s isolate cache, GET only; section 4.5 status uses the outbox, waiting and incidents reads with per-read heads, completeness and page bounds, shows denied, unknown and more, never zero; admin reads stay admin. (2) Section 4.2 allocates eight blobs and six doubles per kind including request and trace IDs, restarts, timed attempts charged, timed entries written and wrote, keeps the turn's end apart from the act's answer, allowlists every blob with fixed route names, drops and counts tainted values rather than truncating, sets a write budget under the platform cap, and states retention, access and cardinality as the boundary. (3) Section 4.4 keeps a server-minted request ID and a validated 32-hex trace ID apart, never stores or echoes tracestate, and asserts neither reaches a grant, key, judge or answer. (4) Correlation is an operational request_index sidecar with an admin-only requests read; section 6 withdraws the Beside member; no entry, outbox row, transport type or replay changes; a throwing, slow or absent sink changes no answer. (5) Section 4.7 weights by _sample_interval, filters by deployed version, requires minimum observations and expected kinds, fails on no-data, stale, query and health, reports coverage, claims no figure. Priority after the demo heads, per Hugh.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:065260027bfbfcdf5f18505ecca31b96aee1acf7","branch":"planner/observability-design","conditions":"Independent exact-head review of 4f0057ac…55ee67